\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.6}{\ignorespaces (a) Illustration of the conversion between right-handed and left-handed circularly polarized light generating a torque on a suspended birefringent half-wave plate. (b) Illustration of transforming a Laguerre–Gaussian (LG) mode carrying OAM $\ell \hslash $ per photon into a mode with $-\ell \hslash $ per photon, which produces a mechanical torque on suspended cylindrical lenses. (c) Demonstration of generating an LG beam with nonzero $\ell $ (left side of bottom row) by introducing a phase shift when converting Hermite–Gaussian modes with zero $\ell $ (left side of top row). All reproduced from Ref.~\blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {allen1992oam}.}}{4}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:SAM_OAM}{{1.6}{4}{(a) Illustration of the conversion between right-handed and left-handed circularly polarized light generating a torque on a suspended birefringent half-wave plate. (b) Illustration of transforming a Laguerre–Gaussian (LG) mode carrying OAM $\ell \hslash $ per photon into a mode with $-\ell \hslash $ per photon, which produces a mechanical torque on suspended cylindrical lenses. (c) Demonstration of generating an LG beam with nonzero $\ell $ (left side of bottom row) by introducing a phase shift when converting Hermite–Gaussian modes with zero $\ell $ (left side of top row). All reproduced from Ref.~\cite {allen1992oam}}{figure.caption.9}{}}
